imgproxy
--------
https://github.com/imgproxy/imgproxy
Copyright (c) 2017 Sergey Alexandrovich and imgproxy contributors
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).

internal/dialect/imgproxy reimplements imgproxy's URL grammar and
processing-option semantics from handlers/path.go (path
redenormalisation), options/parser/url.go (source URL decoding),
options/parser/parse.go and options/parser/apply.go (option argument
rules). The code was rewritten against xtandard-image's own request model
and modified as described in the package documentation.
internal/pipeline/plan reimplements imgproxy's processing geometry from
processing/prepare.go (calcScale, calcSizes, limitScale, CalcCropSize,
angleFlip), processing/scale_on_load.go, processing/crop.go,
processing/calc_position.go, processing/gravity.go (RotateAndFlip),
processing/extend.go, processing/padding.go, processing/fix_size.go,
processing/vector_guard_scale.go, security/checker.go (CheckDimensions)
and imath/. The code was rewritten as a pure planner over xtandard-image's
request model (typed steps instead of in-place libvips calls) and extended
with relative sizes, aspect ratio, adaptive, outside and max-width/height
resizing, as described in the package documentation.
internal/vips/shim.h, shim.c, load.c, image.c, ops.c and save.c contain
portions derived from imgproxy's vips/vips.c,
https://github.com/imgproxy/imgproxy
Copyright (c) 2017 Sergey Alexandrovich
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0,
https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
Modifications (reduced operation set, error capture at the failure site,
refcounted VipsBlob input buffers) are marked in the file headers.

imaginary and bimg
------------------
https://github.com/h2non/imaginary
Copyright (c) 2015-2020 Tomas Aparicio and contributors
https://github.com/h2non/bimg
Copyright (c) Tomas Aparicio and contributors
Both licensed under the MIT License.

internal/dialect/query reimplements imaginary's endpoint and parameter
semantics (image.go, params.go, options.go) and the bimg resize rules
they rely on (resizer.go); internal/security/sign/imaginary.go
reimplements imaginary's URL signature (middleware.go). The code was
rewritten against xtandard-image's own request model.
internal/codec/bmp and internal/codec/ico reimplement in pure Go the BMP and
ICO loaders and savers of imgproxy's vips/bmp.h, vips/bmpload.c,
vips/bmpsave.c, vips/ico.h, vips/icoload.c and vips/icosave.c,
https://github.com/imgproxy/imgproxy
Copyright (c) 2017 Sergey Alexandrovich
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0,
https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
Modifications (OS/2 and V2/V3 headers, arbitrary bitfields, embedded
PNG/JPEG, ICO AND masks, multi-entry ICO output with DIB entries up to
48 px, bounds and pixel-limit checks) are described in the file headers.
The derived portions are the init sequence, cache and concurrency setup,
per-thread cleanup, the save-to-buffer pattern, flatten background scaling
for 16-bit images, trim preparation (sRGB conversion and alpha flattening
before vips_find_trim) and per-frame processing of animated images.
Modifications (one fixed-arity function per operation, options as plain
structs, error capture at the failure site, refcounted VipsBlob input
buffers with decode-failure attribution) are marked in the file headers.
internal/codec/imagemeta (iptc.go, iptc_tags.go) is derived from imgproxy's
imagemeta/iptc/iptc.go, imagemeta/iptc/tags.go and
imagemeta/photoshop/photoshop.go, https://github.com/imgproxy/imgproxy
Copyright (c) 2017 Sergey Alexandrovich
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0,
https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
Modifications (bounds-checked slice parsing, Pascal-string resource names,
raw IIM input, Photoshop resolution decoding) are described in the file
headers; the IPTC dataset table is copied with renamed identifiers.

